&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of dedicated experience designing, building and operating production ETL pipelines at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong programming skills in Python (or a similar language) and SQL; deep hands-on experience with Spark/PySpark. We use Databricks and Delta Lake here&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with workflow orchestration tools such as Airflow, including DAG design, backfills and failure recovery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong data modeling skills for analytics - curated/gold-layer datasets, schema design, partitioning and data contracts consumed by downstream services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ongoing interest in agentic developer workflows: testing agent harnesses, building them, agent loop engineering, and similar emerging paradigms. You enjoy learning how they&#39;re reshaping the way software gets built.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A rigorous approach to data quality: validation, reconciliation and methodology comparison as part of shipping any dataset&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience debugging distributed data systems - performance tuning, memory issues, and optimizations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written communication and cross-functional collaboration skills, from tech specs to incident writeups&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bonus points if you have experience with OLAP stores (e.g., ClickHouse)&lt;/li&gt;
